    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Build a tournament table and merge panels!</strong></i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tournamentris is a completely new merging-style falling block puzzle game based on the theme of \u2018<i>tournament table</i> x <i>falling block puzzle</i>.\u2019</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How to play</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Number panels</strong> rise from the bottom of the board. If the panels overflow the lines on the board, it's game over.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/7d5da33a2ea4b062ae15c8951a714fa9.avif?t=1752655861\" width=800 height=450 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >During the game, players can drop <strong>bridges</strong> and <strong>crowns</strong> from above. By stacking bridges and crowns, a \u2018<strong>tournament</strong>\u2019 is completed, and when a tournament is formed, the panels merge and disappear.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/c7ff3b1382cc9fe1a1f7660825da1297.poster.avif?t=1752655861\" width=800 height=800 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/c7ff3b1382cc9fe1a1f7660825da1297.webm?t=1752655861\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/c7ff3b1382cc9fe1a1f7660825da1297.mp4?t=1752655861\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bridges connect the <u>same numbers</u>, and the connected numbers become the <u>next number</u>. For example:  </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1 + 1 \u2192 2</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >2 + 2 \u2192 3</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >3 + 3 \u2192 1</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(The last two 3s revert to 1.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/827bf23a8dd18fa5a804c495dfa3394b.poster.avif?t=1752655861\" width=800 height=800 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/827bf23a8dd18fa5a804c495dfa3394b.webm?t=1752655861\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/827bf23a8dd18fa5a804c495dfa3394b.mp4?t=1752655861\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Additionally, if the numbers (colours) are the same, you can connect a bridge to a panel (or a bridge to another bridge). This allows you to create a larger tournament.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Strategy</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Make a big tournament!</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When the tournament is complete, the rise will stop for a certain amount of time.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The larger the completed tournament, the longer the stop time.</p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Even if the number of panels cleared is the same, clearing them all at once in a large tournament will result in a higher score.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It also saves crown pieces.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Make the tournament quickly!</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If the bridge pieces overflow from the board, it's game over.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >While creating a large tournament, complete it quickly without crossing the lines and eliminate the pieces.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Make  a beautiful tournament!</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Depending on the shape of the tournament (how the bridges are arranged), special roles such as Orthodox, DanDan, Max, and Full are assigned.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Special-shaped tournaments yield higher scores.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/cc58791c69679e40405b7d0bbfa92c59.avif?t=1752655861\" width=800 height=450 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Future Plans</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to single-player mode, we plan to implement local/online multiplayer mode and puzzle mode.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Build a tournament table and merge panels!</strong></i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tournamentris is a completely new merging-style falling block puzzle game based on the theme of \u2018<i>tournament table</i> x <i>falling block puzzle</i>.\u2019</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How to play</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Number panels</strong> rise from the bottom of the board. If the panels overflow the lines on the board, it's game over.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/7d5da33a2ea4b062ae15c8951a714fa9.avif?t=1752655861\" width=800 height=450 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >During the game, players can drop <strong>bridges</strong> and <strong>crowns</strong> from above. By stacking bridges and crowns, a \u2018<strong>tournament</strong>\u2019 is completed, and when a tournament is formed, the panels merge and disappear.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/c7ff3b1382cc9fe1a1f7660825da1297.poster.avif?t=1752655861\" width=800 height=800 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/c7ff3b1382cc9fe1a1f7660825da1297.webm?t=1752655861\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/c7ff3b1382cc9fe1a1f7660825da1297.mp4?t=1752655861\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bridges connect the <u>same numbers</u>, and the connected numbers become the <u>next number</u>. For example:  </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1 + 1 \u2192 2</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >2 + 2 \u2192 3</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >3 + 3 \u2192 1</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(The last two 3s revert to 1.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/827bf23a8dd18fa5a804c495dfa3394b.poster.avif?t=1752655861\" width=800 height=800 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/827bf23a8dd18fa5a804c495dfa3394b.webm?t=1752655861\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/827bf23a8dd18fa5a804c495dfa3394b.mp4?t=1752655861\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Additionally, if the numbers (colours) are the same, you can connect a bridge to a panel (or a bridge to another bridge). This allows you to create a larger tournament.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Strategy</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Make a big tournament!</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When the tournament is complete, the rise will stop for a certain amount of time.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The larger the completed tournament, the longer the stop time.</p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Even if the number of panels cleared is the same, clearing them all at once in a large tournament will result in a higher score.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It also saves crown pieces.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Make the tournament quickly!</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If the bridge pieces overflow from the board, it's game over.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >While creating a large tournament, complete it quickly without crossing the lines and eliminate the pieces.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Make  a beautiful tournament!</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Depending on the shape of the tournament (how the bridges are arranged), special roles such as Orthodox, DanDan, Max, and Full are assigned.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Special-shaped tournaments yield higher scores.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3849410/extras/cc58791c69679e40405b7d0bbfa92c59.avif?t=1752655861\" width=800 height=450 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Future Plans</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In addition to single-player mode, we plan to implement local/online multiplayer mode and puzzle mode.</p>",
